    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/assistant-director-dual-enrollment.aspx": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Dual Enrollment Matriculation",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Dual Enrollment Matriculation Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Assistant Director of Dual Enrollment Matriculation Assistant Director of Dual Enrollment Matriculation More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Assistant Director of Dual Enrollment Angola, Indiana Full-time Summary The Assistant Director of Dual Enrollment supports the overall administration, coordination,\n                                    and continued growth of Trine University’s Dual Enrollment program. This position\n                                    serves as a key resource for dual enrollment students, families, high school partners,\n                                    faculty, and internal university departments, helping ensure a consistent and positive\n                                    experience throughout the dual enrollment lifecycle. The Assistant Director assists with student and partner support, registration and\n                                    enrollment processes, communications, academic and course-related questions, data\n                                    management, events, program operations, and troubleshooting. The position works closely\n                                    with the Director of Dual Enrollment to strengthen processes, maintain strong relationships\n                                    with partner schools, and support program quality and compliance. The role also supports engagement and matriculation efforts by helping dual enrollment\n                                    students understand opportunities to continue their education at Trine University\n                                    following high school. While recruitment and matriculation are components of the position,\n                                    the primary focus is providing comprehensive support for Dual Enrollment students,\n                                    partners, and program operations. Duties and Responsibilities Dual Enrollment Program Support and Operations Support the day-to-day administration and operation of the Dual Enrollment program. Serve as a resource for students, families, high school partners, faculty, and university\n                                       departments regarding Dual Enrollment policies, processes, timelines, and requirements. Assist with student registration, enrollment, course changes, account questions, and\n                                       other student-related processes. Help identify and resolve issues that may impact the student or partner experience,\n                                       coordinating with appropriate university departments when necessary. Assist with the development, implementation, and documentation of Dual Enrollment\n                                       processes and procedures. Student and Family Support Provide timely and accurate assistance to dual enrollment students and families throughout\n                                       the enrollment process. Help students understand course options, academic expectations, university resources,\n                                       policies, and next steps. Assist students with questions related to registration, course access, technology,\n                                       transcripts, grades, and other aspects of the Dual Enrollment experience. Connect students and families with appropriate university resources when additional\n                                       assistance is needed. Promote a positive student experience by providing consistent communication and proactive\n                                       support. High School Partner Support and Relationship Management Establish and maintain strong relationships with high school counselors, administrators,\n                                       instructors, and other Dual Enrollment partners. Serve as an accessible point of contact for partner schools and assist with questions,\n                                       concerns, and program needs. Provide schools with information and resources related to registration, courses, student\n                                       eligibility, deadlines, policies, and university procedures. Coordinate regular communication and outreach with partner schools. Assist with school visits, meetings, presentations, information sessions, and other\n                                       partner engagement activities. Academic and Course Support Assist students and school partners with questions regarding course selection, academic\n                                       pathways, prerequisites, and Dual Enrollment opportunities. Support communication regarding course offerings, schedules, faculty needs, course\n                                       expectations, and student requirements. Help students understand how Dual Enrollment coursework may apply toward future Trine\n                                       degree programs or other educational pathways. Assist with identifying opportunities to create meaningful academic pathways for partner\n                                       schools and students. Communication and Coordination Develop and coordinate communications to students, families, school partners, and\n                                       other stakeholders throughout the Dual Enrollment cycle. Help ensure information provided through email, websites, registration systems, presentations,\n                                       and other materials remains accurate and consistent. Assist with maintaining Dual Enrollment resources, presentations, training materials,\n                                       and operational documentation. Events and Engagement Assist with the planning, coordination, and execution of Dual Enrollment events both\n                                       on campus and at partner high schools. Support orientations, advising sessions, workshops, classroom presentations, partner\n                                       meetings, and other Dual Enrollment programming. Maintain a presence at partner schools when appropriate to provide students and school\n                                       personnel with direct access to university support. Identify opportunities to increase student awareness of Trine resources, programs,\n                                       and the broader university experience. Engagement and Matriculation Support Help Dual Enrollment students understand opportunities to continue their education\n                                       at Trine University following high school. Provide information about academic programs, admission pathways, transferability of\n                                       Dual Enrollment credits, campus opportunities, and next steps. Collaborate with the Office of Admission on appropriate outreach and engagement strategies\n                                       for Dual Enrollment students who may be interested in matriculating to Trine. Support events and communications designed to introduce Dual Enrollment students to\n                                       additional Trine University opportunities. Track engagement and matriculation outcomes to help evaluate the effectiveness of\n                                       these efforts. Data Management, Reporting and Process Improvement Maintain accurate records related to students, partner schools, courses, communications,\n                                       and program activities. Assist with monitoring enrollment, participation, engagement, and other Dual Enrollment\n                                       metrics. Compile reports and analyze data to identify trends, needs, and opportunities for\n                                       program improvement. Support the development of more efficient processes and systems to improve the student,\n                                       partner, and staff experience. Help ensure appropriate information is documented and shared across departments. Compliance and Accreditation Support Support program practices consistent with university policies and applicable Dual\n                                       Enrollment requirements. Assist the Director of Dual Enrollment with maintaining documentation and processes\n                                       associated with National Alliance of Concurrent Enrollment Partnerships (NACEP) Accreditation\n                                       Standards. Participate in data collection, reporting, documentation, and continuous improvement\n                                       efforts related to accreditation and program quality. Help ensure partner schools, students, and university stakeholders receive consistent\n                                       information regarding program expectations and requirements. Other Duties Perform other duties as assigned in support of the Dual Enrollment program and university\n                                       priorities. Required Education & Experience Bachelor’s degree from a four-year college or university Salary Competitive based on experience. Outstanding Benefits: Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health - medical, dental, flex spending, HSA accounts Life insurance - a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1 ½ times annual salary Paid vacation and sick time Retirement - after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Review of candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\n                                    Candidates should send a letter of interest, a curriculum vitae, detailing all academic\n                                    & professional experience, plus the names, addresses, and telephone numbers of three\n                                    references within their application. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/director-student-design-center.aspx": {
      "title": "Director of the Student Design Center",
      "description": "Director of the Student Design Center | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Director of the Student Design Center Director of the Student Design Center More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Director of the Student Design Center Angola, Indiana Summary The Allen School of Engineering and Computing invites applications for the Student\n                                    Design Center Director. The Director will provide college-wide leadership for engineering\n                                    laboratories and the Student Design Center (SDC). The Director is responsible for\n                                    laboratory safety, technician supervision and prioritization, controlled access, major\n                                    equipment, machining operations, structural testing, large-scale experimental setups,\n                                    and consistent laboratory practices across the Allen School. The Director supports\n                                    academic programs, capstone projects, student organizations, faculty research, and\n                                    approved external projects. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Laboratory Leadership and Staff Supervision — 25% Supervise, coordinate, and evaluate the college’s laboratory technicians. Allocate technical support according to safety, instructional schedules, equipment\n                                       availability, and college priorities. Coordinate laboratory readiness across departments. Develop annual operating, maintenance, and capital-equipment plans. Maintain clear boundaries among technician work, faculty responsibilities, IT, and\n                                       Facilities. SDC Operations and Major Equipment — 25% Direct daily operation of the Student Design Center. Oversee controlled work areas, machining equipment, fabrication systems, reaction\n                                       floor, overhead crane, rigging, structural-testing systems, and other high-risk equipment. Support machining and fabrication primarily for capstone projects and approved student\n                                       organizations. Plan and assist with large-scale mechanical and civil engineering experimental setups. Coordinate equipment installation, commissioning, inspection, preventive maintenance,\n                                       service, and decommissioning in conjunction with laboratory technicians. Manage relationships with vendors, contractors, inspectors, and service providers. Safety, Access, and Compliance — 25% Establish and enforce college-wide laboratory and SDC safety procedures. Develop equipment-specific training and user-certification requirements. Authorize, restrict, or suspend access when unsafe conditions exist. Maintain training, inspection, incident, and equipment-authorization records. Coordinate OSHA-related practices, machine guarding, lockout/tagout, lifting and rigging,\n                                       compressed gases, emergency procedures, and personal protective equipment. Lead incident review and corrective-action processes. Coordinate with Laboratory Safety Committee, Facilities, Security, and other university\n                                       offices. Academic and Project Support — 20% Coordinate technical support for scheduled laboratories, senior design, student organizations,\n                                       research, and approved industry projects. Assist faculty with safe implementation of unusual, large-scale, or high-risk experiments. Provide structured student supervision and equipment guidance in controlled SDC areas. Ensure that experimental setups are feasible, safe, and appropriately scheduled. Administration — 5% Manage assigned budgets, purchasing, inventories, service agreements, and equipment\n                                       records. Prepare utilization, maintenance, safety, and staffing reports. Recommend laboratory policies and capital priorities to the dean. Education and/or Experience REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in engineering, engineering technology, industrial technology, laboratory\n                                       management, occupational safety, or a closely related field. Substantial experience managing engineering laboratories, manufacturing operations,\n                                       technical facilities, or comparable environments. Experience supervising technical personnel and prioritizing work across multiple users. Demonstrated knowledge of machining, fabrication, mechanical testing, equipment maintenance,\n                                       and occupational safety. Ability to communicate effectively with faculty, students, staff, vendors, and contractors. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree or relevant professional certification. Experience in a university engineering environment. Experience with CNC machining, structural testing, cranes and rigging, machine guarding,\n                                             and lockout/tagout. OSHA, first-aid, forklift, crane, rigging, or related safety credentials. Experience developing training, certification, and controlled-access programs. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/enrollment-marketing-event-specialist.aspx": {
      "title": "Enrollment Marketing and Event Specialist",
      "description": "Enrollment Marketing and Event Specialist Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Enrollment Marketing and Event Specialist Enrollment Marketing and Event Specialist More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Enrollment Marketing and Event Specialist Angola, Indiana Summary This role provides marketing, group event planning, communication and project management\n                                    support for the projects, group events and communication plans for the Office of Admission.\n                                    This role requires a strong, demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple priorities,\n                                    deliverables, and timelines. The building and management of project plans are essential\n                                    to the success and support of the admissions and recruitment goals. With leadership\n                                    and support from the VP and AVP, this position collaborates closely with the admissions\n                                    team, the admissions operations team, the various colleges and departments, and the\n                                    University Office of Marketing and Communications. This position must also have a\n                                    broad understanding of appropriate academic programs and potential future directions;\n                                    be flexible, visionary, creative, and energetic and, possess a demonstrated capacity\n                                    to lead. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Develop ADM annual mail grid/timelines for all admission communication projects, including\n                                       digital and print Work with the Office of Marketing and Communications to manage the projects, plans,\n                                       purchase orders, approvals, and timelines Assist in running processes daily out of Slate Analyze data and trends for marketing materials/web content/other Prepares annual reports for the admission office Demonstrates the ability to clean and verify data Assists with third-party processes for bulk mailings and other Review monthly web content for accuracy and makes recommendations on changes and handle\n                                       the updates Handles print collateral inventory requests Back up office manager and enrollment coordinators as needed Be flexible with evening and weekend hours for events Other duties as assigned by the AVP for Enrollment Management Responsible for providing a comprehensive marketing plan to recruit new students through\n                                       the campus visit program, which thoroughly analyzes and assesses Trine’s competitive\n                                       markets and concludes with realistic goal projections for event and individual visit\n                                       attendance. Has responsibility for assisting the Director of Admission in planning, implementation\n                                       and evaluation of all programs and efforts, which seek to enroll an academically talented\n                                       and culturally diverse student body. Preview Day/Scholarship Day: Oversee all administrative, managerial, and performance-based aspects of all Preview\n                                       Day visitation programs and Storm Saturday programs Work with all areas (ex. Athletics, Food Service, AV, Academics, Facilities, and others)\n                                       involved in Preview Days to thoroughly coordinate all aspects of the event Assists with the annual marketing direct-mail grid, working closely with staff in\n                                       implementing mailings on a strategic, timely and cost-efficient basis. Proactively propose new ideas to improve and enhance the visitor experience Provide insight on new ideas to improve and enhance Preview Days and Storm Saturdays. Other duties as assigned Group Visits Team with the Visit Coordinator to create a “best visit ever” experience Coordinates campus group visits and events for students in grades 5–12 and serves\n                                       as the primary point of contact for schools and community organizations. Manage all aspects of group visit planning, including scheduling, agendas, campus\n                                       tours, academic experiences, meals, space reservations, transportation logistics,\n                                       and special requests. Collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and campus partners to develop engaging\n                                       and age-appropriate visit experiences that highlight Trine University’s academic programs,\n                                       student life, facilities, and resources. Maintain accurate group visit records, attendance information, and follow-up documentation\n                                       within appropriate University systems. Assist with evaluating group visit effectiveness, participation trends, and feedback\n                                       to continually improve the campus visit experience. Prepares, reviews, and submits reports as necessary. Other duties as assigned Education and/or Experience Bachelor’s Degree required; prefer three to five years of related experience and/or\n                                    training; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Apply Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/financial-aid-counselor.aspx": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor| Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Financial Aid Counselor Financial Aid Counselor More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Financial Aid Counselor Angola, Indiana Summary The Financial Aid Counselor reports directly to the Director of Financial Aid and\n                                    will assist in all areas of financial aid, including Title IV programs (Direct Loans,\n                                    Pell, TEACH etc.), State Grants, institutional programs, and all other aid as it relates\n                                    to the financial aid program. The Financial Aid Counselor also handles day-to-day\n                                    operations of the Office of Financial Aid that are outlined below. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Financial Aid Counselor works and contributes through a team-oriented approach\n                                    to collaborate with the Director of Financial Aid in the overall planning and operations\n                                    of Trine’s financial aid programs, including Financial Aid Planning, application and\n                                    FAFSA processing, advising, policy and communication development, all direct and private\n                                    loan counseling, processing of private student loan applications, new and current\n                                    student packaging and any other functions deemed necessary to the department. The\n                                    Financial Aid Counselor handles day-to-day operations within the office to include\n                                    reporting to COD, daily ISIR Processing, Title IV Grant programs, and the DL Program.\n                                    In addition to these responsibilities, the Counselor will work collaboratively with\n                                    all areas within the University to enhance and support the financial aid programs;\n                                    and assist the Director in planning, implementation, and evaluation of all programs\n                                    and efforts. Evening hours and weekends may be required as needed, but are minimal.\n                                    Other duties as assigned by the Director are not limited to the following: Counsel students and their families on financial aid processes and procedures, including\n                                       making presentations for orientations, open houses, campus visits etc. Familiarity, assessment, compliance, and communication to the appropriate University\n                                       officers of federal and state financial aid compliance-related issues/policies. Financial Aid packaging to include – Verifications, Loan Certifications, Revisions\n                                       and all other packaging processes related to Financial Aid Ensure federal & state guidelines for student enrollment and financial aid eligibility\n                                       are met Assist with review process for Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) at the end of\n                                       every academic term Perform student “Needs Analysis” Review student files to ensure accurate funding Counsel students to determine financial aid needs /options Ensure compliance with federal & state policies Interact with outside agencies including the DOE and loan processing companies Inventory of materials and print pieces Website review and maintenance Provide direct customer support by routinely visiting with students during new student\n                                       orientation and preview days and any other times that a student needs financial assistance. Answer questions as they arise from students and their families about the financial\n                                       aid process by phone call, email or in person Keep students engaged with the University and supports retention, communication, and\n                                       academic rehabilitation. Perform other duties as assigned Education/Experience Prefer Bachelor’s degree from a four-year college or university, and two or more years\n                                    of successful financial aid/advising or related experience and/or training; or equivalent\n                                    combination of education and experience. Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Benefits offered include: Health – medical, dental, vision, prescription drugs, flex spending or HSA accounts Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for employer contribution\n                                       of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with employee\n                                       life insurance (1½ times annual salary) Education – after 6 months of full-time service, education benefits are available\n                                       for employee, spouse, and dependent children Vacation and Sick Pay – in accordance with Trine's policy Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for\n                                       employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national\n                                       origin, genetic information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis\n                                       prohibited by law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. \n                                       Trine will comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to\n                                       qualified individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/head-coach-acro-tumbling.aspx": {
      "title": "Head Acrobatics & Tumbling Coach",
      "description": "Head Acrobatics & Tumbling Coach | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Head Acrobatics & Tumbling Coach Head Acrobatics & Tumbling Coach More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Head Acrobatics & Tumbling Coach Angola, Indiana Summary: The Head Coach is responsible for planning, managing and evaluating all aspects of\n                                    a particular sport.  Planning, managing, and evaluating the sports program will require\n                                    the head coach to: teach, train, condition, and coach all team members in game strategies\n                                    and techniques. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Lead the program in teaching theoretical skills such as sport psychology and preparation,\n                                       demonstrating and teaching advanced skills for a particular sport, mentoring and advising\n                                       students on personal health and academic matters, organizing and coaching the junior\n                                       varsity program with the assistance of the assistant coach. Lead the program in the identification and recruitment of prospective student-athletes.\n                                       Evaluate prospect pool through attendance at high school or sport organization contests. \n                                       Scout opponents and organize scouting reports.  Maintain accurate and complete recruiting\n                                       records and ensure student-athletes are in compliance with the by-laws of Trine University,\n                                       the conference, and the NCAA. Lead the program in the promotion of the sport program on campus and in the community.\n                                       Lead in fundraising activities, camps, and clinics for the sport and for the entire\n                                       athletic department. Manage and facilitate the recording of sport games/matches. Lead the program in the\n                                       transportation of student-athletes to and from contests. Other duties as assigned by the Athletic Director. Education and Experience Bachelor's degree from a four-year college or university is desired; Master’s degree\n                                    is preferred; a proven record of success in intercollegiate athletics including recruiting\n                                    and Division III experience desired. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/housekeeper.aspx": {
      "title": "Housekeeper",
      "description": "Housekeeper | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers housekeeper Housekeeper More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Housekeeper Angola, Indiana Summary Trine University is seeking full-time 3rd shift housekeepers who will be responsible\n                                    for cleaning and maintaining University buildings and assisting with the setting up\n                                    of summer camps held on the Trine University campus. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Include, but are not limited to: Sweeping, mopping, scrubbing, striping and waxing of floors Washing windows and window sills Select, measure and mix products for cleaning jobs Clean, sanitize and polish restrooms and their fixtures Clean and polish classroom and office furniture Remove waste and debris Replace light bulbs and clean fixtures Set up tables and chairs for special events Stock closets with cleaning and paper products Sweep and shovel walkways 10' from all entrances. Education and/or Experience A High School diploma or General Education Degree (GED) is required. Job Requirements Willingness to perform duties associated with commercial cleaning, including operating\n                                    industrial-type cleaning equipment such as high-speed buffers, scrubbers, and carpet\n                                    cleaners; cleaning restrooms; moving heavy items such as tables and chairs and caring\n                                    for all responsible equipment. To perform this job successfully, an individual must\n                                    be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below\n                                    are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations\n                                    may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Work Environment : While performing the essential functions of this job an employee is occasionally\n                                          exposed to wet, and/or humid conditions; high, precarious places; fumes and/or airborne\n                                          particles; toxic or caustic chemicals; outside weather conditions and vibration. The\n                                          noise level in the work environment is usually moderate. Certificates, Licenses, Registrations : Must maintain a valid driver's license. Physical Demands : The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met\n                                          by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While\n                                          performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand; walk;\n                                          use hands and arms; climb and balance on ladders; stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl; see,\n                                          talk, hear and smell. The employee must be able to lift and/or move up to 50 pounds\n                                          and strong enough to operate industrial-type cleaning equipment. Language Skills : Ability to read and interpret documents such as safety rules, product label instructions,\n                                          operating and maintenance instructions and procedure manuals. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Are you ready to join Trine? Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/campus-safety-officer-part-time.aspx": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Campus Safety Officer | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Campus Safety Officer Part Time Campus Safety Officer More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Campus Safety Officer - Part Time Angola, Indiana Summary This position is responsible for the safety and security of students, visitors, and\n                                    employees, as well as the safety and security of the facilities. The Campus Safety\n                                    Officer supports the needs of the students by being available and responsive. The\n                                    Campus Safety Officer must be customer – service oriented, maintain a professional\n                                    appearance and maintain professional relationship with local authorities. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Assisting students, visitors and staff in accordance with Trine University guidelines. Inform and educate students, visitors and staff within the Trine University guidelines. Pro-actively patrol, as a deterrent to criminal activity or violations of Trine University\n                                       rules. Maintain high visibility during patrol. Look for any hazards to the safety and well-being of students, visitors or staff. Maintain sound public relations, in an effort to support and promote Trine University. Report and document accidents, incidents, and disciplinary issues as required. Cooperate with law enforcement authorities per Trine University guidelines. Carry out other duties, tasks, and responsibilities as may be assigned or directed\n                                       by the Dean of Student Services and/or the Director of Campus Safety. Required Education: High School diploma or General Education Degree (GED) is required. Experience: Must have a flexible schedule. Must possess a valid driver's license and pass a background\n                                    check with no criminal record or serious motor vehicle violations. Salary: The pay is on a part-time hourly basis. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                    regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                    citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                    such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                    its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                    with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/cdl-driver.aspx": {
      "title": "CDL Driver",
      "description": "CDL Driver | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers cdl-driver CDL Driver More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! CDL Driver Angola, Indiana Summary Trine University is seeking part-time seasonal CDL drivers who will be responsible\n                                    for providing transportation for students, faculty, staff and guests of the University\n                                    during the academic year. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Include, but not limited to, the following: ability to drive University provided vehicles\n                                    (cars, vans, bus). Provide transportation to and from area airports (Detroit, Chicago,\n                                    Fort Wayne, South Bend). Provide transportation to athletic events. Provide shuttle\n                                    service from the University to various locations around the Angola area. Qualifications Ability to safely operate or drive cars, vans and bus. Ability to communicate verbally\n                                    and in written form. Ability to assist with loading luggage. Ability to perform safety\n                                    inspections of vehicle. Able to drive during the daylight or night conditions. Education and/or Experience A High School diploma or General Education Degree (GED) is required. Demonstrate driving\n                                    experience of larger profile vehicles. Are you ready to join Trine? Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug"
    },
