    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/help-desk-specialist.aspx": {
      "title": "Help Desk Specialist",
      "description": "Help Desk Specialist Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Help Desk Specialist Help Desk Specialist More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Help Desk Specialist Fort Wayne, Indiana Summary The Help Desk Specialist plays a critical frontline role in delivering exceptional\n                                    technology support to Trine University’s students, faculty, staff, and guests of the\n                                    Brooks College of Health Professions in Fort Wayne, IN. This position is responsible\n                                    for travel to branch campuses in Michigan, Arizona, and Virginia. The Help Desk Specialist\n                                    provides friendly, knowledgeable assistance across a wide range of IT services—serving\n                                    both remotely and in person. The role demands a proactive mindset, strong problem-solving\n                                    skills, and the ability to thrive both independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced\n                                    support environment. This is a full-time, hourly role with a regular schedule of Monday through Friday,\n                                    7:00 AM to 4:00 PM, with occasional evening or weekend hours as needed (and compensated).\n                                    The position reports to the Help Desk Assistant Manager Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide end-user support via phone, email, remote tools, and in-person assistance\n                                       for all campus-supported technologies. Monitor and manage Help Desk tickets: document progress, communicate with stakeholders,\n                                       and ensure timely resolution following departmental guidelines. Troubleshoot and resolve issues related to hardware, software, network access, and\n                                       peripheral devices. Install, configure, and support PCs, printers, software applications, and other hardware\n                                       for end users and campus labs. Support personal devices used by faculty, staff, and students, including basic troubleshooting\n                                       for privately-owned computers. Develop and maintain end-user documentation; deliver training and onboarding sessions\n                                       for students, faculty, and staff. Provide on-site support at off-campus locations using university-provided vehicles. Deliver consistently high-quality service as reflected in customer feedback and service\n                                       level metrics. Supervise morning student workers when the IT Services Assistant Manager is unavailable. Perform other duties or special projects as assigned to support departmental goals. Education and/or Experience Bachelor’s degree in computer science or related field desired, or 2+ years of experience\n                                       in a Technology support role Advanced knowledge and troubleshooting of personal computer technologies. Exposure to Mac workstations in a windows domain. CompTIA A+ Certification desired. Help Desk Institute Certification desired. Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Benefits offered include: Health – medical, dental, vision, prescription drugs, flex spending or HSA accounts Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for employer contribution\n                                       of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with employee\n                                       life insurance (1½ times annual salary) Education – after 6 months of full-time service education benefits are available for\n                                       employee, spouse, and dependent children Vacation and Sick Pay – in accordance with Trine's policy Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for\n                                       employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national\n                                       origin, genetic information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis\n                                       prohibited by law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. \n                                       Trine will comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to\n                                       qualified individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/international-services-processor.aspx": {
      "title": "International Services Processor",
      "description": "International Services Processor Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers International Services Processor International Services Processor More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! International Services Processor Detroit, Michigan Summary The International Services Processor supports the Office of International Services\n                                    by processing immigration-related documentation and maintaining accurate international\n                                    student records in SEVIS and university systems. This position focuses on compliance-based\n                                    processing, data accuracy, and timely updates to ensure the university meets federal\n                                    F-1 regulatory requirements. The International Services Processor serves as a Designated\n                                    School Official (DSO) upon training and works within established procedures under\n                                    supervisory guidance. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) upon training and authorization. Process student requests and updates within Trine University student record platforms. Assist with Curricular Practical Training (CPT) processing by updating student SEVIS\n                                       records and providing updated immigration documents to students. Complete SEVIS registration for F-1 students each academic term. Maintain accurate student data in SEVIS, Sunapsis (or applicable immigration system),\n                                       and the university student information system in accordance with institutional and\n                                       federal record-keeping requirements. Conduct routine audits of assigned student records to ensure data accuracy and federal\n                                       compliance. Identify discrepancies or situations requiring regulatory interpretation and escalate\n                                       to leadership within the Office of International Services. Generate basic compliance and enrollment reports as requested. Additional duties as assigned. Education and/or Experience Required: High school diploma or GED. Preferred: Experience in higher education, records management, data processing, or customer service.\n                                    Experience working with database systems. Experience with international students. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Apply Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/sta-clinical-and-lab-supervisor.aspx": {
      "title": "Surgical Technologist Clinical & Lab Supervisor",
      "description": "Surgical Technologist Clinical & Lab Supervisor | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Surgical Technologist Clinical & Lab Supervisor Surgical Technologist Clinical & Lab Supervisor More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Surgical Technologist Clinical and Lab Supervisor Fort Wayne, Indiana Part-time Summary The STA Clinical and Lab Supervisor will be responsible for overseeing surgical technology\n                                    students at the clinical sites and will support the program through hands on learning\n                                    in the lab. Duties and Responsibilities Supervise students in person at their assigned clinical sites Support instructor of record during lab sections. Responsible for assisting with set\n                                       up, hosting and clean up of weekly labs and lab practicals Promote a collaborative relationship between Trine University and the clinical site\n                                       as a point of contact for the site and students while supervising the clinical. Communicate any changes in policies at the clinical sites to the Program Director\n                                       that impact student learning. Assigns students to cases in order to fulfill programmatic requirements. Advocates for student learning opportunities through communication with clinical sites\n                                       and coordination with program faculty. Supervisor has the opportunity to review learning\n                                       objectives and course sylabi with faculty on a semester basis. Ensures a safe environment for patients, students, and clinical site staff by ensuring\n                                       compliance based on Clinical Affiliation agreement requirements. Makes systematic observations and objective judgments about student performance by\n                                       providing guidance, feedback, and suggestions for improvement. May participate in university seminars and professional development opportunities. Attends programmatic advisory committee meetings. Other duties as assigned Required Education Associate degree in Surgical Technology and Minimum three years’ experience in the operating room in the scrub role or three years of current experience as an instructor of Surgical Technology or A combination of both Possess a current, surgical technology-specific credential that is accredited by the\n                                       National Commission on Certifying Agencies (NCAA) Outstanding Benefits: Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health - medical, dental, flex spending, HSA accounts Life insurance - a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1 ½ times annual salary Paid vacation and sick time Retirement - after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Review of candidates will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/practical-training-processor-phoenix.aspx": {
      "title": "Practical Training Processor",
      "description": "Practical Training Processor Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Practical Training Processor Practical Training Processor More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Practical Training Processor Phoenix, Arizona Summary The Practical Training Processor supports the Practical Training team in processing\n                                       requests and maintaining records for students participating in Curricular Practical\n                                       Training (CPT), Optional Practical Training (OPT), and STEM OPT. This role involves\n                                       working knowledge of F-1 visa regulations related to employment and requires accuracy\n                                       in handling student records, SEVIS updates, and communication. The Practical Training\n                                       Processor serves as a Designated School Official (DSO) and assists in SEVIS registration\n                                       and batch updates as they relate to practical training. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Process CPT, OPT, and STEM OPT requests submitted by F-1 students. Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO). Review and update SEVIS records related to employment authorization. Assist with SEVIS registration and mass updates to records for students on practical\n                                       training. Maintain accurate and up-to-date student records in the student information system\n                                       and SEVIS. Monitor request queues and assist in resolving incomplete or returned e-forms. Collaborate with Practical Training Advisors to support students through practical\n                                       training authorization and reporting processes. Participate in audits and reports on student employment data. Utilize the SEVIS system to pull data related to F-1 student OPT/STEM OPT employment. Stay informed of updates to DHS/SEVP guidance and university policy as it relates\n                                       to student employment. Additional duties as assigned. Education and/or Experience Bachelor’s degree preferred. Preferred: · Experience with international student relations. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Apply Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/student-success-representative-det.aspx": {
      "title": "Student Success Representative",
      "description": "Student Success Representative | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Student Success Representative Student Success Representative More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Student Success Representative Detroit, Michigan Summary The Student Success Representative (SSR) is responsible for delivering professional,\n                                    high-quality support to students at Trine University. This dynamic role requires a\n                                    strong blend of organizational excellence, interpersonal communication, and technological\n                                    proficiency. SSRs serve as critical connectors between students and university resources,\n                                    building positive, collaborative relationships across departments to support student\n                                    success and retention. Ideal candidates will be flexible, creative, visionary, and energetic team players\n                                    who can thrive in a fast-paced environment. The position demands a high degree of\n                                    independence, sound decision-making skills, and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities\n                                    with minimal supervision. Student Success Representatives must be adaptable and solutions-oriented,\n                                    demonstrating a genuine commitment to supporting students through every stage of their\n                                    academic journey. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Serve as the primary point of contact for students, providing guidance and/or directing\n                                       inquiries to the appropriate university staff or departments. Deliver exceptional customer service by responding to student needs with professionalism,\n                                       empathy, and efficiency. Accurately process a variety of student requests according to university policies\n                                       and procedures. Manage and resolve tickets within the ticketing system, ensuring inquiries are documented,\n                                       tracked, and escalated appropriately. Handle a high volume of incoming calls and emails while maintaining responsiveness\n                                       and service quality standards. Meet established performance metrics related to call volume, email response times,\n                                       and resolution efficiency. Perform other duties as assigned in support of student success and departmental operations. Education and/or Experience A minimum high school or GED diploma is required with a minimum of four years of administrative\n                                    support/customer service experience or an associate’s degree preferred. Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for\n                                       employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national\n                                       origin, genetic information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis\n                                       prohibited by law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. \n                                       Trine will comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to\n                                       qualified individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/assistant-associate-professor-civil-engineering.aspx": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Civil Engineering (Transportation)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Civil Engineering (Transportation) | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Assistant/Associate Professor - Civil Engineering (Transportation) Assistant/Associate Professor - Civil Engineering (Transportation) More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Assistant/Associate Professor - Civil Engineering (Transportation) Full-time Angola, Indiana Summary The Reiners Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at Trine University\n                                    invites applications for a full-time faculty position at the rank of Assistant/Associate\n                                    Professor with a preferred start date of August 2026. We seek a dynamic, student-centered\n                                    educator who will contribute to our mission of promoting intellectual and personal\n                                    development through professionally focused and formative learning opportunities. The\n                                    successful candidate will demonstrate a passion for teaching, mentoring, and engaging\n                                    undergraduate students in both classroom and laboratory settings while contributing\n                                    to the continued growth of the civil engineering program. The faculty member will\n                                    be expected to teach transportation engineering courses and support other areas of\n                                    the curriculum based on departmental needs. The candidate will also pursue scholarly\n                                    and professional activities that enhance undergraduate education and strengthen industry\n                                    engagement. Essential Duties and  Responsibilities Teaching and Mentoring Teach undergraduate civil engineering courses, including courses in transportation\n                                       engineering. Teach courses in surveying, geographic information systems (GIS), and/or civil engineering\n                                       materials. Support instruction in foundational civil engineering courses as needed. Develop engaging, hands-on learning experiences that emphasize conceptual understanding,\n                                       problem-solving, and real-world applications. Supervise undergraduate design projects, including capstone design and experiential\n                                       learning activities. Maintain regular office hours and provide thoughtful academic and career advising. Scholarship and Professional Development Engage in scholarly or professional activities consistent with the university’s mission\n                                       and focused on enhancing undergraduate education. Involve undergraduate students in research, applied projects, or scholarly activities. Present scholarly work at conferences and/or publish in relevant journals or engineering\n                                       education venues. Maintain professional engagement through participation in relevant professional societies\n                                       and continuing professional development. Service Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities. Contribute to student recruitment, outreach, and industry engagement initiatives. Support ABET accreditation processes and continuous improvement efforts within the\n                                       civil engineering program. Education and/or Experience Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Civil Engineering or a closely related field required Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentoring excellence. Effective communication skills and ability to work collegially in a collaborative\n                                       academic environment. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the undergraduate level (as instructor, lecturer, or TA). Experience or strong interest in active learning, project-based learning, and laboratory\n                                       instruction. Record or potential for scholarly activity involving undergraduates (applied research,\n                                       curriculum innovation, or engineering education). Applicants should submit Cover letter describing qualifications, teaching interests, and alignment with the\n                                       University’s mission. Curriculum vitae. A two-page statement of teaching philosophy that describes approaches to engaging\n                                       and supporting undergraduate learners. A one-page statement of scholarly interests, highlighting ways to involve undergraduates\n                                       in potential research or applied projects. Contact information for three professional references. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Salary Rank and salary will be based on qualifications. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position\n                                    is filled. Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/assistant-associate-professor-construction.aspx": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Construction Management",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Construction Management | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Assistant/Associate Professor - Construction Management Assistant/Associate Professor - Construction Management More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Assistant/Associate Professor - Construction Management Full-time Angola, Indiana Summary The Reiners Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at Trine University\n                                    invites applications for a full-time faculty position at the rank of Assistant/Associate\n                                    Professor with a preferred start date of July 2027. We seek a dynamic, student-centered\n                                    educator who will contribute to our mission of promoting intellectual and personal\n                                    development through professionally focused and formative learning opportunities. The\n                                    successful candidate will demonstrate a passion for teaching, mentoring, and engaging\n                                    undergraduate students in both classroom and laboratory settings while contributing\n                                    to the continued growth of the construction management and civil engineering programs.\n                                    The faculty member will be expected to teach construction management courses and support\n                                    other areas of the curriculum based on departmental needs, including recruiting students\n                                    for the construction management program. The candidate will also pursue scholarly\n                                    and professional activities that enhance undergraduate education and strengthen industry\n                                    engagement. Essential Duties and  Responsibilities Teaching and Mentoring Teach undergraduate construction management courses. Teach courses in surveying, geographic information systems (GIS), and/or civil engineering\n                                       materials. Support instruction in foundational construction management and civil engineering\n                                       courses as needed. Develop engaging, hands-on learning experiences that emphasize conceptual understanding,\n                                       problem-solving, and real-world applications. Supervise undergraduate design projects, including capstone and experiential learning\n                                       activities. Maintain regular office hours and provide thoughtful academic and career advising. Scholarship and Professional Development Engage in scholarly or professional activities consistent with the university’s mission\n                                       and focused on enhancing undergraduate education. Involve undergraduate students in research, applied projects, or scholarly activities. Present scholarly work at conferences and/or publish in relevant journals or engineering\n                                       education venues. Maintain professional engagement through participation in relevant professional societies\n                                       and continuing professional development. Service Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities. Contribute to student recruitment, outreach, and industry engagement initiatives. Support ACCE and ABET accreditation processes and continuous improvement efforts within\n                                       the construction management and civil engineering programs. Education and/or Experience Required Qualifications M.S. in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a\n                                       closely related field with at least five years of relevant industry experience. Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentoring excellence. Effective communication skills and ability to work collegially in a collaborative\n                                       academic environment. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or\n                                       a closely related field. Teaching experience at the undergraduate level (as instructor, lecturer, or adjunct). Experience or strong interest in active learning, project-based learning, and laboratory\n                                       instruction. Record or potential for scholarly activity involving undergraduates (applied research,\n                                       curriculum innovation, or engineering education). Applicants should submit Cover letter describing qualifications, teaching interests, and alignment with the\n                                       University’s mission. Curriculum vitae. A two-page statement of teaching philosophy that describes approaches to engaging\n                                       and supporting undergraduate learners. A one-page statement of scholarly interests, highlighting ways to involve undergraduates\n                                       in potential research or applied projects. Contact information for three professional references. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Salary Rank and salary will be based on qualifications. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position\n                                    is filled. Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/assistant-professor-nursing.aspx": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Nursing | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Assistant Professor of Nursing Assistant Professor of Nursing More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Assistant Professor of Nursing Angola, Indiana Full-time Summary The position of Assistant/Associate Professor for the Associate of Science in Nursing\n                                    program requires an individual who can provide excellence in teaching, interested\n                                    in both their students and their subjects.  The Assistant / Associate Professor must\n                                    be committed to the centrality of a Trine University education. Reporting to the Director\n                                    of Nursing of the ASN program in the Brooks College of Health Professions, the Assistant/Associate\n                                    Professor should have a broad understanding of appropriate academic programs and potential\n                                    future directions; be flexible, visionary, creative, and energetic; and want students\n                                    to excel and take pleasure in their success. Fair discipline, attention to duty, and\n                                    desire for self-improvement are expected traits of Trine University Faculty members. Duties and Responsibilities Instruction Teach a standard load of 18 contact hours per semester Provide excellence in teaching with adherence to University policies and protocol Post the course syllabus in the learning management system, Moodle, and review with\n                                             students on the first day of class Record class attendance Submit absentee and deficiency information to Academic Support Services via MyPortal Assist students with academic deficiencies Post and maintain a regular schedule of at least ten (10) office hours per week Curriculum development and implementation Participate in the development, implementation, evaluation, and revision of instructional\n                                             material and curricula within the ASN program Utilize the official syllabi of record (SoR) for each course taught Integrate best practices from Quality Matters into courses taught Adhere to the exam guidelines established by the ASN program Provide instruction for the class length listed in the official schedule Program contribution Collaborate with faculty and staff Adhere to the policies and procedures of the ASN program and nursing unit Participate in faculty committee meetings for the nursing unit Support student recruitment, admission, and retention for the ASN program in collaboration\n                                             with the University enrollment staff Participate in advisory board meetings for the nursing unit Participate in the development of the nursing unit’s strategic plan Assist the ASN Director of Nursing in departmental functions Fiscal management of the program Provide input for the preparation and management of the annual budget Utilize the nursing unit’s resources responsibly to facilitate achievement of the\n                                             mission, goals, core values, and expected outcomes Continuous programmatic review and analysis Engage in program evaluation with analysis of data to improve instructional and program\n                                             quality Adherence to University goals, standards, and policies as well as nursing accreditation\n                                             standards and policies Program accreditation processes Collaborate with the Executive Director of Nursing and the ASN Director of Nursing\n                                             in the completion of required accreditation documents for the Indiana State Board\n                                             of Nursing and national nursing accreditor(s) Participate in accreditation documentation and activities as required Perform additional duties and assignments as prescribed by the Executive Director\n                                       of Nursing and the ASN Director of Nursing Required Education A Master of Nursing degree from an accredited university An earned doctorate degree in nursing, education, or a relevant discipline from an\n                                       accredited university is preferred Holds an active, unencumbered registered nurse (RN) license in the State of Indiana\n                                       or in a Nurse Licensure Compact (NLC) state that includes practice privileges in Indiana A minimum of three years’ experience in a full-time academic appointment with teaching\n                                       responsibilities at the associate level is preferred A minimum of three years documented clinical experience as a registered nurse Documented scholarship (e.g., scholarship of application, scholarship of teaching,\n                                       scholarship of integration, and scholarship of discovery) Salary Rank and salary will be based on qualifications. Outstanding Benefits: Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health - medical, dental, flex spending, HSA accounts Life insurance - a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1 ½ times annual salary Paid vacation and sick time Retirement - after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Review of candidates will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/assistant-professor-psychology.aspx": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Psychology | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Assistant Professor - Psychology Assistant Professor of Psychology More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Assistant Professor of Psychology Angola, Indiana Summary: The Department of Psychology invites applications for a full-time assistant professor\n                                    position on campus in Angola, Indiana, starting the Spring semester 2027. We are seeking\n                                    a candidate who is committed to undergraduate instruction -- flexible, creative, and\n                                    energetic with a strong desire to see students succeed. Candidates with a background\n                                    in any area of psychology are urged to apply. Trine University does not offer tenure,\n                                    but contracts are renewed annually, and faculty retention is outstanding Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Teach a broad range of undergraduate courses in psychology. Advise students majoring in psychology. Provide service to the University by serving on committees, advising student groups,\n                                       and assisting with departmental initiatives, etc. Work with the department chair and faculty on program assessment, course and program\n                                       development, and student recruitment. Required education: The ideal candidate will have expertise in and the ability to teach a variety of undergraduate\n                                    courses in the field of psychology.  A doctoral degree in psychology or a related\n                                    field is preferred.  Candidates with masters degrees will also be considered. Outstanding Benefits: Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health - medical, dental, vision,flex spending, HSA accounts Life insurance - a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1 ½ times annual salary Paid sick time Retirement - after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Salary Full-time, faculty-line salary and benefit schedule. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-applied-music.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Applied Music",
      "description": "Adjunct - Applied Music | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Adjunct - Applied Music Adjunct Professor - Applied Music More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor - Applied Music Angola, Indiana Summary: The Trine University Music Program on the Angola, Indiana, campus, invites applications\n                                    for the establishment of an open pool of temporary adjunct faculty positions to teach\n                                    in-person applied music lessons in brass, woodwind, string, vocal, keyboard, and percussion\n                                    for the 2026-2027 academic year.  Appointments are contingent on student enrollment\n                                    and instructional need.  Applications in this pool will only be good for the current\n                                    academic year.  Responsibilities include developing an applied music lesson curriculum\n                                    based on student goals, evaluating and advising student musicianship and technique,\n                                    maintaining accurate records of student progress, and submitting grades according\n                                    to institutional policies. Additional teaching assignments may include directing sectionals with the appropriate\n                                    ensemble and instrument section (marching/pep band, wind ensemble, chamber orchestra,\n                                    university choir, and jazz bands) in consultation with the Director of the Music program. Applicants must have a master’s degree in music performance; experience working with\n                                    a wide range of musical skill levels and styles from beginner, intermediate, and advanced;\n                                    and/or four years of successful applied teaching experience at the community, university,\n                                    or professional level plus a bachelor’s degree in music performance.  Professional\n                                    music performance experience is preferred, but not required. For consideration, please submit a letter of interest addressing relevant expertise\n                                    and experience; a curriculum vitae containing names and contact information for three\n                                    references; and copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Salary Salary is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-chemistry.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Chemistry",
      "description": "Adjunct - Chemistry | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Chemistry Adjunct in Chemistry More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor - Chemistry Lab Angola, Indiana Summary Teaching responsibilities will focus on general chemistry.  Salary is based on the\n                                    number of credit hours taught. Candidates must have earned a Bachelor's Degree in Chemistry with teaching experience\n                                    preferred. The Department of Science at Trine University is a part of the Rinker-Ross School\n                                    of Health Sciences, and offers B.S degrees in chemistry, biochemistry, biology, and\n                                    forensic science.  The department is housed in the Best Hall of Science and has recently\n                                    moved into a new $6.6 million, 26,000 square-foot addition.  The addition includes\n                                    new biochemistry, organic, and physical/inorganic chemistry laboratories as well as\n                                    space for student research.  The department is well equipped with modern instrumentation\n                                    for both teaching and research, with significant additions including: three GCs, GCMS,\n                                    HPLC, microwave plasma spectrometer, FTIR, and NMR (60 MHz) with multi-element probe,\n                                    having been made within the last five years. Applicants should send a detailed CV, a letter describing their qualifications for\n                                    teaching laboratories and copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Required Education Candidates must have teaching experience and have completed graduate work in chemistry. Salary Salary is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
