    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-forensic-science.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Forensic Science",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor - Forensic Science | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Adjunct Professor - Forensic Science Adjunct Professor - Forensic Science More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor - Forensic Science Angola, Indiana Summary Teaching responsibilities will focus on forensic science. Salary is based on the number\n                                    of credit hours taught. Candidates must have earned a bachelor's degree in forensic science, chemistry, biochemistry,\n                                    or biology with teaching experience preferred. The Department of Science at Trine University is a part of the Rinker Ross School\n                                    of Health Sciences, and offers B.S. degrees in chemistry, biochemistry, biology, and\n                                    forensic science. The department is located in Best Hall of Science, home of new anatomy\n                                    and physiology, microbiology, biochemistry, organic, and physical/inorganic chemistry\n                                    laboratories as well as space for student research. Additionally, the Best Hall of\n                                    Science recently completed a $16 million, 36,000 square-foot addition. This addition\n                                    includes new physical/inorganic chemistry laboratories, quantitative/instrumental\n                                    chemistry laboratories, a collaborative learning classroom, faculty offices, and renovated\n                                    molecular biology and biochemistry laboratories. The department is well equipped with\n                                    modern instrumentation including two Anatomage tables, a Synergy HTX multi-more plate\n                                    reader, BSL-II microbiology teaching lab, inverted and fluorescent microscopes, a\n                                    genetics facility (nanodrop, genetic analyzer, thermocycler, and electroporator),\n                                    and numerous chemistry analytical instrumentation. Applicants should send a detailed CV, a letter describing their qualifications for\n                                    teaching courses/laboratories and copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Required Education Candidates must have expertise in the field of forensic science and/or complete graduate\n                                    work in their respective fields. Salary Salary is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-faculty-humanities-and-communication.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Humanities and Communication",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Humanities and Communication | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Humanities and Communication Adjunct Professor - Humanities and Communication More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor - Humanities and Communication Angola, Indiana Summary Trine University's Department of Humanities and Communication is currently accepting\n                                    applications for Adjunct Faculty to teach a variety of courses, including academic\n                                    and professional writing, speech, communication and foreign language. This position teaches on-site, seated courses at Trine's Angola, Indiana campus. We accept applications for this part-time role year-round. Applicants will be reviewed\n                                       and contacted as openings become available. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching Commitment to serving students Excellent oral communication and interpersonal skills Excellent written communication skills Required Education and Experience Candidates must have teaching experience and have completed a Master's degree in a\n                                       related field. Salary Salary is prorated based on the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Candidates should apply online with the following: a letter of interest, a curriculum\n                                    vita detailing all academic and professional experience, (unofficial) graduate transcripts,\n                                    and the contact information. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis  prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to  qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-jazz-show-ensemble.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Jazz/Show Choir Ensemble",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor - Jazz/Show Choir Ensemble | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Adjunct - Jazz/Show Choir Ensemble Adjunct Professor - Jazz/Show Choir Ensemble More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor - Jazz/Show Choir Ensemble Part Time Angola, Indiana Summary: The Trine University Music Program seeks a dynamic adjunct faculty member to lead\n                                    the Jazz/Show Choir Ensemble beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Direct the Jazz/Show Choir in twice-weekly rehearsals, teaching proper diction, vowels,\n                                       articulations, rhythms, intonation, vocal blend and balance, and color. Provide instruction to students with a wide range of musical backgrounds. Determine repertoire, prepare, and lead the ensemble in at least one public performance\n                                       each semester. Hold ensemble placement auditions for voice at the beginning of each semester. Manage and organize Jazz/Show Choir Ensemble sheet music and uniforms. Attend Music Program department meetings. Work with the Director of the Music program on concert scheduling, program production,\n                                       and logistics. Additional teaching assignments may include teaching applied music lessons in voice\n                                    in consultation with the Director of the Music program. Education and/or Experience: Preferred: Master's degree in vocal performance and Experience working with a wide range of musical skill levels and styles, from beginner,\n                                             intermediate, and advanced. Required: Bachelor's degree in music. Five years of experience in ensemble direction or teaching experience at the community,\n                                             university, or professional level. Music performance experience. For consideration, please submit a letter of interest addressing relevant expertise\n                                    and experience; a curriculum vitae containing names and contact information for three\n                                    references; copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and links to two (2)\n                                    video examples of contrasting vocal jazz styles. Review of applications will begin immediately, and applications will be accepted until\n                                    the position is filled. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-music-athletic-band.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Music & Athletic Band",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor - Music & Athletic Band | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Adjunct - Music & Athletic Band Adjunct Professor - Music & Athletic Band More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor - Music & Athletic Band Part Time Angola, Indiana Summary: The Trine University Music Program seeks an adjunct faculty for the academic year\n                                    2026-2027. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Instruct instrument sections (brass, woodwind, or drumline) based on the candidate’s\n                                       area of expertise and teach drill for the Trine University Sound of Thunder Marching\n                                       Band and Pep Band during rehearsals. Teach courses within the Music Program, such as music theory or history or applied\n                                       studies in music as applicable to the candidate’s expertise or as assigned by the\n                                       Music Director. Provide instructional leadership for the Sound of Thunder Marching Band and Pep Band\n                                       by directing rehearsals and performances in the Director of Music’s absence, ensuring\n                                       continuity in musical pedagogy, ensemble development, and student learning during\n                                       home football, men’s and women’s basketball and select hockey games. Develop instructional drill materials for pregame and halftime performances, creating\n                                       educationally grounded marching formations that support student musicians’ technical\n                                       growth, spatial awareness, and performance proficiency. Participate in recruitment activities for the Music Program as part of student outreach\n                                       and educational engagement, representing instrumental ensembles (jazz, chamber orchestra,\n                                       wind ensemble, marching/pep band) at SOAR, Preview Days, Band Day, and Honor Band\n                                       events, and providing prospective students with academic guidance in the absence of\n                                       the Director of Music. Support the instructional operations of the music program through academic administration,\n                                       including coordination of learning materials, planning student-centered events, and\n                                       managing instructional resources (instruments, uniforms, and sheet music) necessary\n                                       for effective teaching and ensemble learning within the Sound of Thunder Marching\n                                       Band and Pep Band. Education and/or Experience: Successful experience with marching and pep bands (collegiate preferred), including\n                                       experience with drill writing, marching techniques, choreography, and instrument instruction\n                                       (brass, woodwind, or drumline). Evidence of success in program administration, recruiting and retention, event planning,\n                                       and inventory management. Minimum of 3 years of successful teaching at the high school or collegiate level. A master’s degree in music performance, music education, or conducting. Candidates should submit a cover letter addressing the qualifications specific to\n                                    this position, a curriculum vitae, links to representative drill writing with performance\n                                    video, and the names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately, and applications will be accepted until\n                                    the position is filled. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-asn.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - ASN",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor - ASN | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Adjunct Professor - ASN Adjunct Professor - ASN More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor - ASN Part Time Angola, Indiana Summary: Adjunct faculty have the responsibility for providing instruction in the ASN program. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Responsible for creating a positive learning environment that prepares students for\n                                       the complexities of today’s workplace Promote intellectual and personal development through personally focused learning\n                                       opportunities, preparing students to succeed, lead and serve Perform duties including, but not limited to, the instruction and education of students Support student recruitment and retention efforts Work collegially with administrators and fellow Educators. Contribute to the development, review, and revision of program policies Qualifications: Required: Registered Nurse with a minimum of three years practice experience Possess an active, unencumbered Registered Nurse license Possess a Master’s degree or higher in nursing (MSN) Demonstrated experience in nursing education Other: Proficiency in Microsoft Office is required, including Word, Excel, Power Point, and\n                                       Outlook; proficiency in Moodle is preferred To perform this job successfully, a candidate will have excellent written and oral\n                                       communication skills. The candidate will be able to adapt to new technology and have\n                                       good time management, organization, and project management skills.  Being detailed\n                                       oriented is necessary. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform\n                                       essential functions Applicants should send a detailed CV, and a letter describing their qualifications. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
