    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-psychology.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Psychology",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor - Psychology | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Adjunct Professor – Psychology Adjunct Professor – Psychology More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor – Psychology Angola, Indiana Summary: The Psychology and Social Sciences Department is now accepting applications for a\n                                    part-time position teaching on the main campus in Angola. Teaching responsibilities\n                                    will focus on 1 or 2 sections of Principles of Psychology. This position requires\n                                    in-person instruction located at Trine University's main campus in Angola, Indiana. We accept applications for this part-time role year-round. Applicants will be reviewed\n                                       and contacted as openings become available. Applicants should send a detailed CV, a letter describing their qualifications for\n                                    teaching the classes and copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Education and Experience Candidates must have at minimum a Master’s degree in Psychology or in a closely related\n                                    field. Salary Salary is is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
