    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/assistant-professor-dpt.aspx": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Physical Therapy | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Assistant/Associate Professor of Physical Therapy Assistant/Associate Professor of Physical Therapy More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Assistant/Associate Professor of Physical Therapy Fort Wayne, Indiana Summary The Trine University Doctor of Physical Therapy program in Fort Wayne, IN, seeks an\n                                    individual with expertise in teaching graduate physical therapy students. Depending\n                                    on individual qualifications, opportunities exist to teach foundational topics of\n                                    physical therapy practice or specific practice areas such as integumentary care, orthopedics,\n                                    or cardiopulmonary rehabilitation. This is a full-time, 12-month position with a preferred\n                                    start date of August 2026. Responsibilities As a core member of the DPT program faculty, the successful candidate will be responsible\n                                    for teaching, advising, mentoring students, participating in scholarship and service\n                                    activities, and assisting with program assessment. Qualifications Terminal academic doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DSc) in a field related to physical therapy Eligibility for licensure as a physical therapist in Indiana. Evidence of ability to effectively conduct research and peer-reviewed dissemination\n                                       of findings. Demonstrated current expertise in physical therapy. Education and/or Experience Terminal academic doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DSc) in a field related to physical therapy A record of successful teaching and scholarship Minimum 3 years of full-time post-licensure clinical practice Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Benefits offered include: Health – medical, dental, vision, prescription drugs, flex spending or HSA accounts Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for employer contribution\n                                       of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with employee\n                                       life insurance (1½ times annual salary) Education – after 6 months of full-time service education benefits are available for\n                                       employee, spouse, and dependent children Vacation and Sick Pay – in accordance with Trine's policy Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is\n                                    filled. Trine University reserves the right to verify academic (transcripts) and professional\n                                    credentials prior to extending offers of employment.  Please include a cover letter,\n                                    resume/CV, and references when applying. Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/assistant-professor-pa-educator.aspx": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/PA Educator",
      "description": "Assistant Professor/PA Educator | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Assistant Professor/PA Educator Assistant Professor/PA Educator More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Assistant Professor/PA Educator, Physician Assistant Fort Wayne, Indiana Part-time Summary The position of PA educator requires an individual who can provide excellence in teaching,\n                                    with interest in both their students and their subject matter. A PA educator must\n                                    be committed to the centrality of a Trine University education and possess the ability\n                                    to support the program in achieving excellence through teaching, scholarship, outreach,\n                                    and engagement. The position of PA Educator will hold faculty rank of an Assistant\n                                    Professor within the MPAS program. Under the direction of the MPAS Program Director,\n                                    PA Educators will be responsible for creating and implementing program curriculum\n                                    and will participate in the ongoing ARC-PA accreditation process. PA Educators will\n                                    provide service to the university, community, and the PA profession, while fully supporting\n                                    Trine's mission of preparing students to succeed, lead, and serve Responsibilities Developing, reviewing and revising as necessary: the mission statement, goals and competencies of the program the program curriculum and course content course goals, learning outcomes, and instructional objectives Selecting applicants for admission to the PA program Providing student instruction to provide students with the necessary attention and\n                                       instruction to acquire the knowledge, skills, and competencies required for entry\n                                       into the profession Evaluating student performance assess and supervise the student's progress in achieving competencies and in fulfilling\n                                       course goals, learning outcomes, and instructional objectives Academic counseling of students providing both academic and professionalism mentoring Student Success Committee activities assuring the availability of remedial instruction, Assisting with continuous programmatic review and analysis to assess data to improve\n                                       instructional and program quality Implement the program’s strategic plan Adherence to University goals, standards and policies as well as ARC-PA Standards\n                                       and ARC-PA policies Principal Faculty must : Teach at least 9 credit hours annually per 12-month contract post and maintain office hours (5 hours per week) not participate as health care providers for students in the program, except in an\n                                                   emergency situation attend faculty meetings and participate in faculty committees including program strategic\n                                                   plan and accreditation Principal Faculty will: promote PA program and PA profession to potential students and community contribute to the Trine University's greater community with scholarship and service\n                                       leading to professional growth and development, which may include publications, presentations,\n                                       participation in conferences and seminars perform additional duties and assignments as prescribed by the Program Director, Dean\n                                                   and/or the Vice President for the College of Health Professions. Education and/or Experience Must be qualified through academic preparation and/or experience to teach assigned\n                                       subjects A physician assistant with a master’s degree, doctoral-level preferred, a current\n                                       NCCPA certification and eligibility for licensure in Indiana A bachelor’s degree will be considered based on work experience OR: a Certified Nurse Practitioner with experience in graduate level teaching and a minimum\n                                                   of two years clinical experience. a physician with current eligibility or unrestricted license as an allopathic or osteopathic\n                                                   physician in Indiana, certified by an ABMS or AOA approved specialty board a PhD basic scientist or hold other academic/doctoral qualifications and relevant\n                                                   academic/clinical experience and fit into the mix of the other professionals of the\n                                                   developing program. In addition: must possess knowledge of the PA profession and be able to effectively advocate for\n                                                   the PA program and profession must have a minimum of two years of clinical experience should have a minimum of two years higher education experience Must maintain licensure in state of Indiana Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is\n                                    filled. Projected starting date can be immediate. Trine University reserves the right\n                                    to verify academic (transcripts) and professional credentials prior to extending offers\n                                    of employment.  Please include a cover letter, resume/CV, and references when applying. Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
