    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-pa.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor - Physician Assistant Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Adjunct Professor - Physician Assistant Adjunct Professor - Physician Assistant More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor -  Physician Assistant Fort Wayne, Indiana Summary: The position of PA Adjunct Faculty demands an individual dedicated to delivering exceptional\n                                    teaching, fostering student engagement, and demonstrating expertise in their subject\n                                    matter. Faculty must be committed to the centrality of a Trine University education\n                                    and possess the ability to support the program in achieving excellence through teaching.\n                                    Under the direction of the MPAS Program Director,  adjunct faculty will be responsible\n                                    for creating and implementing the program curriculum by supporting Trine's mission\n                                    of preparing students to succeed, lead, and serve. Essential Responsibilities: Adjunct Faculty must be responsible for, and actively participate in the processes of: Provide student instruction, ensuring learning goals and competencies are met Develop engaging and informative course content aligned with program objectives. provide students with the necessary attention and instruction to: acquire the knowledge, skills, and competencies required for entry into the profession Evaluating student performance evaluate student performance, assessing competencies, course goals, learning outcomes,\n                                       and objectives. Academic support for students be available at least by email to answer questions related to course content assuring the availability of remedial instruction Required Education Adjunct Faculty must be: qualified through academic preparation and/or experience teaching knowledgeable in course content assigned subjects a physician assistant with a master’s degree preferred current NCCPA certification Adjunct Faculty alternatively may be: a Certified Nurse Practitioner with experience in graduate-level teaching a physician with current eligibility or unrestricted license as an allopathic or osteopathic\n                                             physician in Indiana, certified by an ABMS or AOA approved specialty board a PhD basic scientist or hold other academic/doctoral qualifications and relevant\n                                             academic/clinical experience and fit into the mix of the other professionals of the\n                                             developing program. In addition, Adjunct Faculty: must possess knowledge of the PA profession and be able to effectively advocate for\n                                             the PA program and profession must have a minimum of two years of clinical experience Salary Salary is based upon credit hours and course enrollment. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is\n                                    filled. Projected starting date can be immediate. Trine University reserves the right\n                                    to verify academic (transcripts) and professional credentials prior to extending offers\n                                    of employment.  Please include a cover letter, resume/CV, and references when applying Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/doctoral-adjunct-professors-detroit.aspx": {
      "title": "Doctoral Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid Detroit, Michigan Summary Trine University invites applications for part-time adjunct positions. Applications are accepted on an ongoing basis to support program and enrollment growth.\n                                    Applications are active for one year from the submission date. Hybrid adjunct faculty\n                                    professor positions is for online faculty who will travel to our Detroit, Michigan\n                                    location once per eight-week term, per course (this is subject to change). The Adjunct Faculty Role The University’s mission is to promote intellectual and personal development through\n                                    personally focused learning opportunities, preparing students to succeed, lead and\n                                    serve. Our faculty are responsible for ensuring students are successful in the online\n                                    classroom and are prepared for the complexities of today’s workplace. It is expected that adjunct faculty will: Actively engage students through frequent interaction and convey a genuine enthusiasm\n                                       for their learning. Provide thorough and constructive feedback, utilizing rubrics to effectively assess\n                                       learners’ work, while also acknowledging learner accomplishments. Demonstrate relevant and current subject-matter expertise and help students connect\n                                       concepts across their academic program. Work effectively with the TrineOnline team to seek continuous improvement for all\n                                       TrineOnline courses and programs. Adjunct Faculty Training All new faculty teaching online are required to successfully complete onboarding training\n                                    as a condition of hire. Required Education A terminal degree from an accredited institution of higher learning with a minimum\n                                       of 18 graduate credit hours in the academic field is preferred Extensive professional experience in a related field Minimum technology requirements must be met, those can be viewed at: https://www.trine.edu/online/student-support/technology.aspx Previous experience teaching online students at the university level Salary Salary is is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Adjunct faculty candidates are required to provide official transcripts during the\n                                    candidate selection process. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/doctoral-adjunct-professors-phoenix.aspx": {
      "title": "Doctoral Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid Phoenix, Arizona Summary Trine University invites applications for part-time adjunct positions. Applications are accepted on an ongoing basis to support program and enrollment growth.\n                                    Applications are active for one year from the submission date. Hybrid adjunct faculty\n                                    professor positions is for online faculty who will travel to our Phoenix, Arizona\n                                    location once per eight-week term, per course (this is subject to change). The Adjunct Faculty Role The University’s mission is to promote intellectual and personal development through\n                                    personally focused learning opportunities, preparing students to succeed, lead and\n                                    serve. Our faculty are responsible for ensuring students are successful in the online\n                                    classroom and are prepared for the complexities of today’s workplace. It is expected that adjunct faculty will: Actively engage students through frequent interaction and convey a genuine enthusiasm\n                                       for their learning. Provide thorough and constructive feedback, utilizing rubrics to effectively assess\n                                       learners’ work, while also acknowledging learner accomplishments. Demonstrate relevant and current subject-matter expertise and help students connect\n                                       concepts across their academic program. Work effectively with the TrineOnline team to seek continuous improvement for all\n                                       TrineOnline courses and programs. Adjunct Faculty Training All new faculty teaching online are required to successfully complete onboarding training\n                                    as a condition of hire. Required Education A terminal degree from an accredited institution of higher learning with a minimum\n                                       of 18 graduate credit hours in the academic field is preferred Extensive professional experience in a related field Minimum technology requirements must be met, those can be viewed at: https://www.trine.edu/online/student-support/technology.aspx Previous experience teaching online students at the university level Salary Salary is is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Adjunct faculty candidates are required to provide official transcripts during the\n                                    candidate selection process. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
